  "title": "editcap: Free the wtap_rec (and thus its buffer) on exit",
  "description": "Call wtap_rec_cleanup() instead of wtap_rec_reset() when\nexiting, so that it gets called in the error path, instead\nof only calling it when there is no error.\n\nOtherwise ASAN/LSAN will complain about leaks when there are\nerrors:\n\n```\n==402786==ERROR: LeakSanitizer: detected memory leaks\n\nDirect leak of 1051648 byte(s) in 1 object(s) allocated from:\n    #0 0x55fb9d09e240 in realloc (/home/johnthacker/wireshark-qt6-clang-build/run/editcap+0xa7240) (BuildId: edeaa1c28aa59d5605e83520b5a5f1fcef5b250a)\n    #1 0x7fcea622ab0a in g_realloc (/lib64/libglib-2.0.so.0+0x48b0a) (BuildId: 2932f63ee7c53ae67d9b0b3ff877ece14c13edd5)\n    #2 0x7fcea6365968 in ws_buffer_assure_space /home/johnthacker/wireshark/wsutil/buffer.c:98:27\n    #3 0x7fcea683c609 in wtap_full_file_read_file /home/johnthacker/wireshark/wiretap/wtap.c:2140:3\n    #4 0x7fcea683c24d in wtap_full_file_read /home/johnthacker/wireshark/wiretap/wtap.c:2179:9\n    #5 0x7fcea683a8ad in wtap_read /home/johnthacker/wireshark/wiretap/wtap.c:1862:7\n    #6 0x55fb9d0e718b in main /home/johnthacker/wireshark/editcap.c:2219:12\n    #7 0x7fcea5efd5b4 in __libc_start_call_main (/lib64/libc.so.6+0x35b4) (BuildId: ff0267465bc3d76e21003b3bc5598fd5ee63e261)\n    #8 0x7fcea5efd667 in __libc_start_main@GLIBC_2.2.5 (/lib64/libc.so.6+0x3667) (BuildId: ff0267465bc3d76e21003b3bc5598fd5ee63e261)\n    #9 0x55fb9cff8944 in _start (/home/johnthacker/wireshark-qt6-clang-build/run/editcap+0x1944) (BuildId: edeaa1c28aa59d5605e83520b5a5f1fcef5b250a)\n\nDirect leak of 2048 byte(s) in 1 object(s) allocated from:\n    #0 0x55fb9d09de38 in malloc (/home/johnthacker/wireshark-qt6-clang-build/run/editcap+0xa6e38) (BuildId: edeaa1c28aa59d5605e83520b5a5f1fcef5b250a)\n    #1 0x7fcea6229c69 in g_malloc (/lib64/libglib-2.0.so.0+0x47c69) (BuildId: 2932f63ee7c53ae67d9b0b3ff877ece14c13edd5)\n    #2 0x7fcea63650cc in ws_buffer_init /home/johnthacker/wireshark/wsutil/buffer.c:33:29\n    #3 0x7fcea683b65b in wtap_rec_init /home/johnthacker/wireshark/wiretap/wtap.c:2001:2\n    #4 0x55fb9d0e7163 in main /home/johnthacker/wireshark/editcap.c:2218:5\n    #5 0x7fcea5efd5b4 in __libc_start_call_main (/lib64/libc.so.6+0x35b4) (BuildId: ff0267465bc3d76e21003b3bc5598fd5ee63e261)\n    #6 0x7fcea5efd667 in __libc_start_main@GLIBC_2.2.5 (/lib64/libc.so.6+0x3667) (BuildId: ff0267465bc3d76e21003b3bc5598fd5ee63e261)\n    #7 0x55fb9cff8944 in _start (/home/johnthacker/wireshark-qt6-clang-build/run/editcap+0x1944) (BuildId: edeaa1c28aa59d5605e83520b5a5f1fcef5b250a)\n\nSUMMARY: AddressSanitizer: 1053696 byte(s) leaked in 2 allocation(s).\n```\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
